; Colour a status bar row: A for the first B-1 cells, blue for the rest
;
; Stores C attribute bytes along one attribute row. The first B-1 cells get A (hearts or crosses owned), every following cell gets blue ink on black paper (the empty slots). Used by #R$9BF3 and #R$9C1B.
; .
; Hardware: writes the attribute file.
;
; A Attribute of the first B-1 cells
; B Number of cells to colour with A, plus one
; C Number of cells in the row
; HL Attribute address of the first cell
@label=FillHudAttrs
c$9C47 DJNZ $9C4B    ; DJNZ falls through when B reaches 0: switch colour
@isub=LD A,BLUE
 $9C49 LD A,$01      ;
*$9C4B LD (HL),A     ; B wraps to $FF afterwards: DJNZ never falls through again
 $9C4C INC L         ;
 $9C4D DEC C         ;
 $9C4E JR NZ,$9C47   ;
 $9C50 RET           ;
